we strongly believe that health is an  essential determinant and component of  well-being improved health status has a  positive impact on other aspects of  well-being such as educational  achievement and labor market  participation the potential savings for  society go well beyond the direct  effects on tp'ed GDP growth we also  discussed about Europe European  pharmaceutical policy that topic had a  really interesting discussion  safeguarding access to many medicines is  a challenging challenge requiring  measures both at the EU level and also  in the Member States  so duties and withdrawals of all  medicines pose a risk to patient safety  and increase the workload of health care  stop this morning during our discussions  are highlighted three priority areas to  the ministers which in my view are  particularly important the first one is  the area that has to do with cancer  arian the priority for myself very  important a huge burden on the economy  huge burden of citizens but most of all  it causes a great deal of suffering as  we all know I have informed the  minister's that I am glad to announce  that on February 4th which is World  Cancer day I will start an inclusive  discussion based on the Europe beating  cancer plan secondly I informed  ministers that I will work to create a  European health data space to maximize  the potential of digital technologies in  health  and this can be a true game changer for  our cancer plan because fighting cancer  without opening borders for services and  health data will not work it really is  imperative that this finally receives  the attention that it it deserves people  too often with mental health problems  are living in silence or are forgotten  and mental health needs to be understood  as a cornerstone as part of the economy  of well-being my mission is to try and  bring all stakeholders together on board  CERN to improve accessibility and  affordability of medicines in this  respect I really do need to emphasize my  thanks to Minister cure for her efforts  in the council to advanced than the  negotiations over the Commission's  health technology assessment proposal  this proposal is vital if we are going  to move forward and it does affect the  policy area of shortages of medicines
 

